Yes. A function can have both cron and event triggers, up to 10 unique triggers per function. Put them all in the `triggers` array [1]:

```ts
inngest.createFunction(
  {
    id: "resync-user-data",
    triggers: [
      { event: "user.created" },
      { cron: "0 5 * * *" },
    ],
  },
  async ({ event, step }) => {
    // ...
  },
);
```

If you tried to define them as two separate trigger arguments or two separate keys, that won't work. Everything goes in the one `triggers` list. Go and Python have equivalents (`MultipleTriggers` and `trigger=[...]`) [1].

In the handler, use `event.name` to tell what fired the run. Cron runs arrive as `inngest/scheduled.timer`, and the function can also be called via `step.invoke()` as `inngest/function.invoked` [3][9]:

```ts
if (event.name === "inngest/scheduled.timer") { /* cron */ }
```

If you're on an older SDK version that took the trigger as a second argument, multi-trigger support was added in inngest-js via an array of triggers there, e.g. `[{ event: "a" }, { cron: "..." }]` [9]. Upgrading is the safest path if the object form is rejected.

control.text:
Yes. A single Inngest function can have multiple triggers, including both a cron and an event. Pass an array to the `triggers` option in the function config (v3+ SDK):

```ts
inngest.createFunction(
  { id: "sync-data" },
  [
    { cron: "0 * * * *" },
    { event: "app/sync.requested" },
  ],
  async ({ event, step }) => {
    // ...
  }
);
```

Things to know:
- The function runs when either trigger fires.
- On cron runs, `event.name` is `inngest/scheduled.timer`, so you can branch on it if the logic differs by trigger.
- Event-only fields like `event.data` won't be populated with your payload on cron runs, so don't assume they exist.
- If you're on an older SDK, check the version: multiple triggers are only supported in newer releases. In v4 the triggers are defined inside the options object as `triggers: [...]`, so check the exact shape against your installed SDK version.

If you're still getting an error defining both, send the SDK version and the exact error message.

